{
  "_doc": [
    "Visual Studio 2022 / 2026 install manifest for myCad contributors.",
    "",
    "Spec: docs/architecture/08-vs-toolchain.md §8.2.1",
    "",
    "Usage:",
    "  1. Open Visual Studio Installer",
    "  2. Click 'More' on your VS instance -> 'Import configuration'",
    "  3. Select this file (tools/vs2022.vsconfig) and confirm",
    "  4. Installer will tick all required components and offer to install missing ones",
    "",
    "Component IDs are stable across VS 17 (2022) and VS 18 (2026). The file works",
    "for both — VS Installer maps IDs to the version-specific package automatically.",
    "",
    "Why each component:",
    "  Workload.NativeDesktop          — base C++ workload; without it, MSVC won't even install",
    "  VC.Tools.x86.x64                — the actual MSVC compiler/linker/STL (v143 / v144)",
    "  VC.CoreIde                      — VS C++ IDE features (project tree, IntelliSense)",
    "  VC.CMake.Project                — CMake support inside VS (preset picker, generator)",
    "  VC.TestAdapterForCatch2         — Catch2 tests show up in VS Test Explorer",
    "  VC.DiagnosticTools              — Profiler, memory usage, debug-time perf views",
    "  VC.ATL                          — required by some vcpkg ports (Qt6, OCCT chain)",
    "  Windows11SDK.26100              — Windows 11 SDK; vcpkg's Qt6 needs SDK >= 22000",
    "  VC.Llvm.Clang                   — Clang for Windows (clang-format / clang-tidy)",
    "  VC.Llvm.ClangToolset            — clang-cl integration for v143/v144 toolset",
    "  Workload.NativeCrossPlat        — Linux/WSL remote dev; lets you build the Linux preset locally",
    "  Linux.CMake                     — CMake-over-WSL/SSH plumbing",
    "  Git                             — bundled Git for Windows (used by .githooks/* and vcpkg)",
    "",
    "Recommended marketplace extensions (NOT in vsconfig — install separately via VS Installer 'Extensions' tab):",
    "  - Markdown Editor v2",
    "  - GitHub Copilot",
    "  - Clang Power Tools",
    "  - VsVim (taste-dependent)",
    "",
    "Explicitly NOT included (per docs §8.2.3): 'Qt Visual Studio Tools'.",
    "Qt is integrated through CMake AUTOMOC/AUTOUIC + vcpkg-installed Qt Designer."
  ],
  "version": "1.0",
  "components": [
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Workload.NativeDesktop",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.Tools.x86.x64",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.CoreIde",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.CMake.Project",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.TestAdapterForCatch2",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.DiagnosticTools",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.ATL",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.Redist.14.Latest",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.Windows11SDK.26100",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.Llvm.Clang",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.Llvm.ClangToolset",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Workload.NativeCrossPlat",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.Linux.CMake",
    "Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.Git"
  ],
  "extensions": []
}
